From: phpv <https://github.com/supanadit/phpv>
Subject: [PATCH] restore LHASH for PHP 5.0/5.1 against OpenSSL 1.0.x

OpenSSL 1.0.x renamed the old LHASH typedef to _LHASH, but PHP 5.0 and
5.1's ext/openssl still declares LHASH pointers. Add the compatibility
typedef after the OpenSSL includes so phpv's pinned OpenSSL 1.0.1u can
build these versions.
---
--- a/ext/openssl/openssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/openssl.c
@@ -43,6 +43,10 @@
 #include <openssl/rand.h>
 #include <openssl/ssl.h>
 
+/* OpenSSL 1.0.x renamed LHASH to _LHASH; PHP 5.0/5.1 still uses LHASH. */
+#include <openssl/lhash.h>
+typedef _LHASH LHASH;
+
 #define DEFAULT_KEY_LENGTH	512
 #define MIN_KEY_LENGTH		384
 
